    cuda: update the KVarN tile calls to the current process_tile signature
    
    Both KVarN call sites in fattn-mma-kvarn-case.cuh still passed the
    argument list from before compact causal masking added
    causal_prefix_first_bound_smem, so they supplied 26 arguments to a
    27-parameter function and GGML_CUDA_KVARN=ON failed to compile here with
    
      error: no instance of function template
      "flash_attn_ext_f16_process_tile" matches the argument list
    
    Both sites pass compact_causal_prefix = false, so the new parameter takes
    nullptr: this path does not use a compact causal bound. There is one
    definition of the function (fattn-mma-f16.cuh:1252) and the two remaining
    callers in that file already pass the parameter, so this brings the KVarN
    instances back in line with them rather than changing any behaviour.
    
    Only the KVarN instances are affected, and they are compiled only under
    GGML_CUDA_KVARN=ON, which is off by default.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E8bBMKTLSzVbDBSUfdQc9N

